From d75e47477ac36ca6ad9e2499ce058ea9a2930251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aression <lvdifine@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:30:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(engine): score centering for the vLLM backend and the
 agent transport

Add Score Centering (arXiv:2609.20807) to AReaL's vLLM rollout backend on
Ascend, carrying the sampler's per-token top-k ids and log-probabilities through
the OpenAI agent transport that `gsm8k_rl.py` uses here, and applying the
additive drift correction in FSDP training.

The calculation is the one merged on `main`: `areal/utils/score_centering.py` is
byte-identical to upstream, the correction is computed engine-side and handed to
the loss as a scalar, and token-level TIS reuses the existing
`rejection_sampling` configuration with no new YAML knob.  What this commit adds
on top:

- a vLLM response parser that accepts both the <= 0.23 flat `top_logprobs`
  layout and the >= 0.30 per-position nested layout (the Ascend images ship
  0.30), plus the `max_logprobs` raise needed to request 128 alternatives;
- head propagation through `ArealOpenAI` / `InteractionWithTokenLogpReward`, so
  the agent transport carries the heads the way the native SGLang path does on
  `main`;
- two opt-in extensions for ablation runs: `sc_loss_mode` ("reinforce" = Plan A
  default, "ppo_additive" = Plan B; a plain str because OmegaConf rejects Literal
  annotations) and
  `sc_reinforce_baseline` (pure REINFORCE while SC is off);
- config guards that reject the combinations this transport cannot support:
  non-FSDP actors, non-vLLM rollouts, tree training, tensor/context parallel,
  temperature != 1, truncated or penalised sampling, distillation, and the other
  policy surrogates (SAPO/CISPO/M2PO/decoupled PPO).  The documented
  `score_centering_top_k` range is enforced by the upstream `validate_sampling`
  helper at load time.

Packed-sequence masking is a separate defect and ships in its own PR; this
branch keeps the upstream mask handling.  TP/CP score centering is not part of
this port either: the vLLM transport cannot hand the trainer sharded heads, so
the engine rejects those layouts and the TP/CP test files are not carried over.

Validation (Ascend 910B, CPU-level suites plus runtime smoke):

- `tests/test_score_centering*.py` and the adjacent suites: 100 passed,
  35 skipped, 1 xfailed.  The skips are the CUDA-gated cases of the adopted
  upstream files; no test is skipped unconditionally.  Two new CPU tests pin
  the load-time sampling guards and the distillation rejection.
- FSDP suite (`tests/test_fsdp_*.py`): 20 passed / 9 failed / 11 skipped, and
  the same cases fail on the unmodified base commit, i.e. they are pre-existing
  NPU gaps rather than regressions from this commit.
- Runtime smoke (Qwen2.5-1.5B, GSM8K, 2 dies, sampler weight noise 0.02/seed 42):
  every step reports `sc_active=1`, `loss_mode=1`, `rs_upper=2.0` and a non-zero,
  stable `sc_correction`.
- Not run: multi-node, Megatron, MoE, virtual pipeline, multimodal, the
  paper-style Countdown reproduction, `pre-commit run --all-files` (ruff
  check/format were run directly: clean), and the docs site build.

Known limitations: an absent top-k slot still gathers a trainer log-probability,
so padded positions rely on `loss_mask` alignment; `rho` is unbounded when a row
carries no head mass (also true upstream); the head width is capped at k, so the
(k+1)-th alternative can be dropped; `validate_sampling`'s SGLang-oriented branch
is unused here.
